{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 36, :comments ["<b>From the heavens, etc.</b> The intention of the verse is, according to what I explained in parashat Yitro at the verse ״וַיְדַבֵּר אֱלֹהִים״ (Exodus 20:1), and which I noted upon it above at the verse (Deuteronomy 4:12) ״וּתְמוּנָה אֵינְכֶם רֹאִים״ etc., it fits well, for the Ten Commandments came to them in two stages, in this manner: the two commandments, which are ״אָנֹכִי״ and ״לֹא יִהְיֶה לְךָ״, the matter reached Israel from HaShem to them through the power of the words and their overwhelming force. Corresponding to these He said <b>מִן הַשָּׁמַיִם הִשְׁמִיעֲךָ אֶת קוֹלוֹ</b>, and the phrase <b>לְיַסְּרֶךָּ</b> means: to purge your impurity — this was the cause of removing from them all zuhama, as I have written many times. And the remaining eight commandments, which complete the ten, they heard from the words themselves that went forth from the Master, blessed be He. Corresponding to these He said <b>וְעַל הָאָרֶץ הֶרְאֲךָ אֶת אִשּׁוֹ</b> — this is the seeing of the voices, which were flames of fire engraved by the word of HaShem, and Israel saw them, as it is written (Exodus 20:15) ״וְכָל הָעָם רֹאִים אֶת הַקּוֹלוֹת״, and as I explained at the verse (Deuteronomy 4:12) ״וּתְמוּנָה״ etc." "And the verse's saying <b>וּדְבָרָיו שָׁמַעְתָּ מִתּוֹךְ הָאֵשׁ</b>, according to our words it fits precisely, for the eight commandments they heard from amidst the aforementioned fire, which is an angel of blazing fire, and as I explained at the verse (Deuteronomy 4:12) ״וּתְמוּנָה״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 4, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:15:15.401265106Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}